.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR Apache-2.0
.TH CCMAKE 1 "2026-11-27" "rcmake 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccmake \- interactive terminal cache editor provided by rcmake
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccmake
.RI [ options ]
.I path-to-source
.br
.B ccmake
.RI [ options ]
.I path-to-existing-build
.br
.B ccmake
.RI [ options ]
.B \-S
.I path-to-source
.B \-B
.I path-to-build
.br
.B rcmake ccmake
.RI [ options ]
.I path-to-source
|
.I path-to-existing-build
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ccmake
is a clean-room Rust interactive terminal cache editor matching CMake 4.5.1
.BR ccmake .
It is built into the multi-call
.B rcmake
binary with no
.B ncurses
or
.B unsafe
code dependencies, and starts through the
.B ccmake
symlink or as
.BR "rcmake ccmake" .
.PP
The editor runs configure and generate in two separate phases over a retained
in-process session.
Pressing
.B c
saves queued cache edits into
.I CMakeCache.txt
and runs configure without writing build files.
Once a configure succeeds with no new cache entries, pressing
.B g
generates the build system from the retained configure session and exits.
Diagnostics and inherited child process output streams go into a bounded
scrollback buffer, and child standard input binds to the null device so
configure commands never corrupt the terminal display.
Terminal raw mode is restored on exit and on unexpected termination.
.PP
.B ccmake
requires an interactive Unix terminal (macOS or Linux) of at least 65 columns
by 6 rows.
Windows is not yet supported in
.BR "rcmake 0.2.1" .
When invoked with no arguments,
.B ccmake
prints short usage text and exits with status 0.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-S " path-to-source"
Explicitly specify the source directory.
.TP
.BI \-B " path-to-build"
Explicitly specify the build directory.
.TP
.BI \-C " initial-cache"
Preload a script to populate the cache before configuring.
.TP
.BI \-D " var" "[:" type "]=" value
Create or update a CMake cache entry.
.TP
.BI \-U " globbing-expr"
Remove matching entries from the CMake cache.
.TP
.BI \-G " generator-name"
Select a build system generator
.RB ( Ninja ,
.BR "Ninja Multi-Config" ,
.BR "Unix Makefiles" ,
or
.B Xcode
on macOS).
.TP
.BI \-T " toolset-name"
Specify the generator toolset where supported.
.TP
.BI \-A " platform-name"
Specify the generator platform where supported.
.TP
.BI \-\-toolchain " file"
Specify a toolchain file
.RB ( CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE ).
.TP
.BI \-\-install-prefix " dir"
Specify the installation prefix
.RB ( CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX ).
.TP
.BI \-\-project-file " name"
Specify an alternate top-level project listfile name.
.TP
.BI \-W category "\fR, \fP" \-Wno- category "\fR, \fP" \-Werror= category "\fR, \fP" \-Wno-error= category
Enable, suppress, or promote diagnostic warning categories.
.TP
.B \-debug
Accepted and ignored for compatibility with upstream CMake 4.5.1.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-H ", " \-\-help ", " \-\-version [ =json-v1 ] ", " \-\-help-*
Print usage, version information
.RB ( "ccmake version 4.5.1"
and
.BR "rcmake 0.2.1" ),
or bundled CMake 4.5.1 reference topics.
.PP
Matching upstream CMake 4.5.1,
.B ccmake
never deletes an existing
.I CMakeCache.txt
before starting, so
.B \-\-fresh
has no effect.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.SS Navigation
.TP
.BR Up ", " k ", " Ctrl-p
Move to the previous cache entry.
.TP
.BR Down ", " j ", " Ctrl-n
Move to the next cache entry.
.TP
.BR PageUp ", " Ctrl-u
Move to the previous page.
.TP
.BR PageDown ", " Ctrl-d
Move to the next page.
.TP
.BR Home ", " End
Jump to the first or last visible entry.
.SS Editing
.TP
.B Enter
Toggle a
.B BOOL
entry, advance an enumerated
.B STRINGS
entry, or edit a text,
.BR PATH ,
or
.B FILEPATH
entry.
While editing,
.B Enter
confirms the change and
.B Esc
cancels it.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle a
.B BOOL
entry.
.TP
.B i
Edit a non-boolean text or path entry.
.TP
.BR Left ", " Ctrl-b ", " Right ", " Ctrl-f
Cycle backward or forward through values listed in the entry's
.B STRINGS
property.
.TP
.B Tab
Complete directory and file names while editing a
.B PATH
or
.B FILEPATH
entry.
.TP
.B d
Delete the selected cache entry.
.SS Search and actions
.TP
.B /
Search cache entry names and values.
Press
.B Enter
to jump to the first match or
.B Esc
to cancel.
.TP
.BR n ", " N
Jump to the next or previous search match.
.TP
.B t
Toggle display of advanced cache entries.
.TP
.B c
Save pending edits and run configure.
.TP
.B g
Generate build files from the retained configure session and exit.
Available only after a configure succeeds with no new cache entries.
.TP
.BR l ", " w
Open the captured configure or generate output log.
.TP
.B h
Open the help screen showing key bindings and the selected entry's help text.
.TP
.B e
Exit the log or help screen and return to the cache list.
.TP
.BR q ", " Ctrl-c
Quit without generating.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RCMAKE_ORACLE_MODE
Set to
.B 1
to disable native
.B rcmake
subcommands, including
.BR "rcmake ccmake" .
Invoking through the
.B ccmake
symlink always runs in compatibility mode.
.TP
.B RCMAKE_VENDORED_DATA_ROOT
Override the directory containing bundled CMake 4.5.1
.IR Modules/ ,
.IR Templates/ ,
and
.I Help/
files.
.TP
.B CMAKE_GENERATOR
Default build system generator when
.B \-G
is omitted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The user exited normally, generation completed, or usage, version, or help
output succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Standard output is not an interactive terminal, the terminal is smaller than 65
columns by 6 rows, the platform does not support the TUI, or loading the cache
failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I CMakeCache.txt
Cache file loaded on startup and updated when configuring.
.TP
.I CMakeLists.txt
Top-level project listfile configured by the session.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure an existing build directory interactively.
.PP
.EX
ccmake -B build
.EE
.PP
Start an out-of-source Ninja configure from a source tree.
.PP
.EX
ccmake -S . -B build -G Ninja
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rcmake (1),
.BR cmake (1),
.BR ctest (1),
.BR cpack (1)
